# Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io), seeded by
# swarm-routing/.github org-sync (`citation = true`; `citation_type` and
# `[[references]]` in .github/org-sync.toml); the repository's own once
# written. Commitizen keeps `version:` in step (`.cz.toml` version_files
# "CITATION.cff:^version:"); swarm-routing/.github tools/zenodo reads the
# concept DOI from `doi:` once the first release is archived on Zenodo.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "POSANT"
abstract: >-
  POSANT, position-based ant colony routing, as a standalone swarm routing
  protocol for geographic and 3D networks (UAVs, FANETs, GPS-equipped outdoor
  meshes): a simulator-agnostic C++23 core on swarm-core's ports with thin
  ns-3 and Linux adapters (planned).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Joppi
    given-names: Daniel Henrique
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6436-8174"
version: "0.0.0"
# The work as a whole; core/ also MIT OR GPL-2.0-only (LICENSING.md).
license: GPL-2.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/swarm-routing/POSANT"
url: "https://github.com/swarm-routing/POSANT"
references:
  - type: article
    title: "A Position Based Ant Colony Routing Algorithm for Mobile Ad-hoc Networks"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Kamali"
        given-names: "Shahab"
      - family-names: "Opatrny"
        given-names: "Jaroslav"
    journal: "Journal of Networks"
    volume: "3"
    issue: "4"
    year: 2008
    publisher:
      name: "Academy Publisher"
    doi: "10.4304/jnw.3.4.31-41"
    notes: "The journal version of POSANT, the primary source this repository implements (swarm-routing/.github#672, decision 18)."
